[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
ESP-IDF is installed in:

  %%ESPRESSIF_IDF_PATH%%

Nothing is added to your PATH automatically.  In each shell in which you
want to build ESP32 projects, run:

  . %%ESPRESSIF_PREFIX%%/esp-idf-env.sh

This sets IDF_PATH and puts %%ESPRESSIF_IDF_PATH%%/tools
(which contains idf.py) in your PATH.  Espressif's own export.sh in that
directory works too.

One-time setup per user:

  %%ESPRESSIF_IDF_PATH%%/install.sh esp32

FreeBSD is not a supported ESP-IDF host.  install.sh downloads Linux
toolchain binaries that will not run here, so you also need a native
xtensa-esp32-elf toolchain in your PATH.

Script interpreters in the installed tree were rewritten to the system
Python.  If you use the virtualenv that install.sh creates, do not rely on
the shebang of idf.py; run it through the virtualenv's Python instead:

  python %%ESPRESSIF_IDF_PATH%%/tools/idf.py build

USB serial ports appear as /dev/cuaU* on FreeBSD, not /dev/ttyUSB*, and
are accessible to members of the "dialer" group:

  idf.py set-target esp32
  idf.py build
  idf.py -p /dev/cuaU0 flash monitor
EOM
}
]
